    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (2/2 passing, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`LocalityLookup.java`** \u2014 added a postcode-range table (NSW 2000\u20112099, VIC 3000\u20113099, QLD 4000\u20114099) and a new overload `regionOf(String city, String postcode)` that:\n1. Looks up the region by postcode range first.\n2. Falls back to the existing city\u2011to\u2011region table only when the postcode is absent or in no known range.\n\nThe single-arg `regionOf(String)` is kept unchanged, so `PostcodeRegions.isValidFor` (which validates a postcode against the *city's* region) is unaffected.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `LocalityLookup.regionOf(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney + postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) while disambiguating via postcode \u2014 an unknown city with a VIC\u2011range postcode (3000) now correctly resolves to VIC, as the new tests assert.",
