    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, in-order sequence for `POST /api/owners`, taken from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class it wires.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Caller lacking that role is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 403) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Validations & normalizations (no transaction yet)\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerRequiredFields`** \u2014 binds the request body once (`@RequestBody`, *not* `@Valid`).\n   - **Side-effect:** normalizes `address` in place first (`AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n   - **Validation:** requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (after normalization), `city`, `telephone` all non-blank. Any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, `errors` array). Republishes the DTO for later steps.\n\n2. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 **side-effect:** rewrites `telephone` to E.164 in place. **Validation:** must clean to 8\u201315 digits; `+61` requires exactly 9 national digits, `+1` exactly 10; otherwise `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n3. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 email is optional. If null/blank, left as-is. If present: **validation** against a syntactic regex (`InvalidEmailException`, 400 on failure); **side-effect:** stored back trimmed and lower-cased.\n\n4. **`ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 postcode optional. If present: must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city in a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099 via `LocalityLookup`/`PostcodeRegions`) must fall in range; else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). No mutation \u2014 value stored as given. Unknown regions accept any 4-digit code.\n\n5. **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 duplicate check. Builds `identityKey = E164 telephone | email(or empty) | prospectiveHouseholdId` and scans all owners; an exact full-key match \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409). (Household id here is only non-empty if `sharesHousehold` is true and a last-name+address match exists.)\n\n6. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); `\u2265 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n7. **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** \u2014 computes effective registration business day (supplied date or `now()`, weekend rolled to Monday) and counts existing owners with that registration date; `\u2265 100` \u2192 `TooManyOwnersTodayException` (429).\n\n## Build & side-effects (all under `govern: [ transaction ]`, committed once at the end)\n\n8. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`). *(transaction starts here)*\n\n9. **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold` is true and an existing owner shares the normalized last name + address:\n   - **Side-effect on the new owner:** sets `householdId` (SHA-256-derived).\n   - **Side-effect on *other* rows:** saves each existing household member that didn't already carry the id (writes to other owners).\n\n10. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` (1 if no household, else existing members + 1).\n\n11. **`ApplyRegistrationDate`** \u2014 sets `registrationDate` to supplied-or-`now()`, rolled forward off weekends to Monday.\n\n12. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is (owners already in that city) + 1.\n\n13. **`AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (last two digits of the registration year).\n\n14. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of pre-existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n15. **`AssignMembershipLevel`** \u2014 sets `membershipLevel` = 1, +1 if email present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3.\n\n16. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if more than 80 owners already share this owner's business-day registration date.\n\n17. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the new owner (assigns its id).\n\n18. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`).\n\n19. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n## Notes\n- Ordering is deliberate: required-field validation precedes the duplicate/capacity/limit checks, which all precede entity construction \u2014 so a bad body yields 400 before any 409/429.\n- The only checks that ever write are steps 8\u201318 (inside the transaction); step 9 is the one place a create can also modify **other** owner rows.\n- Steps 5\u20137, 14, 16 each do a full `ownerRepository.findAll()` scan (repeated O(n) passes over all owners per create)."
